// THE DOM THE LAYOUT GUARD LAYS OUT (layoutFloor.test.ts, lots 28-29): each box as the
// running app rendered it on a phone held sideways (740x360) and upright (360x740) -
// the inline composer with a quote and two attachments (once with three lines typed,
// once dictating while files upload: its live hypothesis and the upload's progress),
// the full-page prompt with the same, the detached composer with three quotes (once
// with the live hypothesis), the report-a-problem dialog, the session settings sheet;
// and the thread with what sits above the composer - the gateway's banner, two queued
// messages, the agent's pending approval, each and all together. Its text is filler of
// the same length; nothing of a conversation or a person is kept. Captured with the
// audit harness (l29CaptureAll); the states a test bench cannot raise (a banner, a
// queue, a dictation, an upload) are the components' markup. Recapture when the markup
// of these boxes changes - the guard checks that every class it relies on is still
// rendered by the components.

